#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186082936 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "74677256-e307-5d49-b7e0-c3f4e79cf818" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Number of Ways That N Objects Can Be Arranged"}] :question/id #uuid "d39c9a9a-e44b-5673-b930-25576c8a54a3" :question/math-academy-id "e-5671" :question/problem "Suppose there are five books on a bookshelf. How many possible ways can we arrange them?" :question/worked-solution "There are $n=5$ books, so the number of possible arrangements is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n5! &= 5 \\cdot 4 \\cdot 3 \\cdot 2 \\cdot 1 \\\\\n&= 120\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, there are $120$ ways of arranging the $5$ books."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186082937 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e49e2595-62a1-595a-8df9-99541bccbdf5" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Permutations"}] :question/id #uuid "0b1ea0d9-4329-562d-b83a-3a6870536a39" :question/math-academy-id "e-5672" :question/problem "How many permutations are there of the letters in the word \"MUSICAL\"?" :question/worked-solution "In the word \"MUSICAL\" there are a total of $7$ letters with no repeat letters, and so there are $7$! ways of arranging them:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n7! &= 7 \\cdot 6 \\cdot 5 \\cdot 4 \\cdot 3 \\cdot 2 \\cdot 1 \\\\\n&= 5040\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, there are $5\\,040$ possible arrangements of the letters of the word \"MUSICAL.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186243615 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "74677256-e307-5d49-b7e0-c3f4e79cf818" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Number of Ways That N Objects Can Be Arranged"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "64ebb59b-c7a1-5c08-ad54-82c6600dd59a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "40,320" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243617} {:answer/id #uuid "1256ae0a-3e14-56ad-b7c2-714176ec5dbc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5,040" :db/id #edb/ref 17592